WEBVTT

00:02:07.877 --> 00:02:10.255
<i>Taking advantage of
the trouble in Pittsburgh,</i>

00:02:10.338 --> 00:02:14.050
<i>The Union of Justice headquarters
was robbed.</i>

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:18.555
<i>But the stolen item was
quickly retrieved by Praetorian.</i>

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:22.809
<i>Praetorian's recent activity
has really been quite brilliant!</i>

00:02:22.892 --> 00:02:27.021
<i>My daughter's bedroom
is plastered with Praetorian posters.</i>

00:02:27.105 --> 00:02:29.607
<i>Don't get jealous of those superheroes.</i>

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:31.442
<i>You don't stand a chance against them!</i>

00:02:41.286 --> 00:02:43.204
That guy ain't no superhero!

00:02:43.288 --> 00:02:47.417
That bum's in cahoots with Matts!
He's just a downright thug!

00:02:51.963 --> 00:02:53.006
I'm takin' a leak.

00:02:53.089 --> 00:02:55.341
We need to get revenge on that guy!

00:02:55.425 --> 00:02:56.676
You sure talk big.

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:08.021
Gramps, slow down.

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:10.398
Shut up!

00:03:11.065 --> 00:03:12.358
Pour me another right now!

00:03:12.942 --> 00:03:15.111
That's right!
I ain't letting them get away with this!

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:17.697
What are we gonna do

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:20.325
now that Orlok got rubbed out
and the helmet was taken back?

00:03:20.408 --> 00:03:22.035
We didn't even get a cent.

00:03:22.619 --> 00:03:25.622
We're no match for Matts and Praetorian.

00:03:26.289 --> 00:03:29.459
Can you grow back
if your brains have been blown up?

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.544
If my brains have been blown up?

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:35.548
My jaw grew back when it got ripped off.

00:03:35.632 --> 00:03:38.092
This is why I hate working with
a team that I can't choose.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.845
How can you say that when we rescued--

00:03:40.929 --> 00:03:42.931
I never asked you to rescue me.

00:03:43.514 --> 00:03:44.474
How dare you!

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.475
What?

00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:49.520
This is so depressing,
I'm about to lose my mind.

00:03:51.105 --> 00:03:52.273
So long.

00:03:53.149 --> 00:03:56.694
Thanks for getting my hopes up
that I might see 50 million dollars,

00:03:56.778 --> 00:03:57.654
Carmine.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.324
I had low expectations from the start.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:05.119
A ragtag group of obscure villains
could never outsmart superheroes.

00:04:09.499 --> 00:04:12.043
If you're leaving,
then get the fuck outta here, jerk!

00:04:12.126 --> 00:04:15.546
Nobody wants to hear you lecture us!

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.215
That was close!

00:04:17.298 --> 00:04:21.135
You just about chopped
Mr. Handsome's face in half!

00:04:26.641 --> 00:04:28.726
Now you've asked for it!

00:04:30.061 --> 00:04:31.354
Hey! Come on, you guys!

00:04:48.329 --> 00:04:49.831
Wait! Kasey!

00:04:56.754 --> 00:04:58.131
-Forecast!
-Cut it out!

00:04:58.214 --> 00:04:59.549
Fine!

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:02.385
All right already, Forecast!

00:05:04.887 --> 00:05:07.557
<i>What do you have to say
to villains across the country?</i>

00:05:08.266 --> 00:05:11.394
<i>There is no place
for you villains in the USA.</i>

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:16.941
<i>Your fate is to grow old and die
as despised and forgotten people.</i>

00:05:17.525 --> 00:05:22.322
<i>We will never let up on you people
until you're utterly eliminated.</i>

00:05:22.905 --> 00:05:27.910
<i>You scum will disappear from this earth
without leaving a single trace.</i>

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.329
<i>Wow! How reassuring!</i>

00:05:29.954 --> 00:05:32.332
<i>That was Praetorian! Thank you!</i>

00:06:02.737 --> 00:06:06.032
I'm in the newspapers…

00:06:07.283 --> 00:06:08.242
Carmine.

00:06:08.326 --> 00:06:09.535
Only when he got caught.

00:06:09.619 --> 00:06:13.206
Jeez! I've banned him so many times,
but he keeps coming back.

00:06:13.289 --> 00:06:17.877
This was supposed to be
the biggest job ever for gramps.

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:20.296
That'll never happen.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:22.965
This loser has never
made it past being a petty thief.

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:25.468
Hanging around him will only hurt you.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:26.385
Before you leave,

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:31.015
you'll pay for his drinks
and to clean up this place, right?

00:06:57.375 --> 00:07:00.419
It's been a while
since I drove this truck.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.631
No way! That burger joint closed down?

00:07:04.215 --> 00:07:07.218
Damn! I never even ate there once.

00:07:13.224 --> 00:07:15.059
This song's one of your favorites, right?

00:07:27.029 --> 00:07:28.072
Honey…

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.285
Dammit!

00:07:32.368 --> 00:07:34.537
How come things never go right?

00:07:35.913 --> 00:07:39.250
I've waited forever for this!
So why did this happen?

00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:41.377
I even went to night school!

00:07:42.044 --> 00:07:43.629
I'm such a total idiot!

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:46.674
I've had it!

00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:22.418
Even if we're not villains,
I want to be with you forever.

00:08:25.254 --> 00:08:27.673
Even if we're never offered
a big job again,

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:30.009
let's live together happily.

00:08:31.761 --> 00:08:32.637
Are you serious?

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:35.515
Where's the ring?

00:08:44.315 --> 00:08:48.069
Kasey, will you marry me?

00:08:49.278 --> 00:08:52.990
You're only saying that
because you saw this church.

00:08:53.074 --> 00:08:55.243
Sorry to interrupt you
at a time like this,

00:08:55.326 --> 00:08:57.745
but this church is
going to be torn down soon!

00:08:58.579 --> 00:08:59.997
Perfect timing.

00:09:00.581 --> 00:09:01.958
Let's throw away our pasts

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:05.503
and live ordinary,
respectable lives together.

00:09:55.219 --> 00:09:56.262
Honey?

00:09:57.638 --> 00:09:58.681
Coming!

00:10:00.474 --> 00:10:03.394
If this is the wedding decoration,
take them directly to…

00:10:05.605 --> 00:10:06.439
What?

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:08.107
Whatever…

00:10:15.323 --> 00:10:17.658
Tonight's your last night
as a single man, Johnny!

00:10:17.742 --> 00:10:18.784
Yeah!

00:10:20.286 --> 00:10:21.370
What?

00:10:27.752 --> 00:10:30.171
We don't serve villains here.

00:10:36.636 --> 00:10:37.511
You scammed us!

00:10:37.595 --> 00:10:39.347
That dude was
doing the dancing the whole time!

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:41.015
This is exactly why

00:10:41.891 --> 00:10:45.603
you can't trust
any business run by villains!

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:51.108
If I don't get home, my baby will--

00:10:51.192 --> 00:10:54.570
Transmit says
he still hasn't had enough to drink.

00:10:54.654 --> 00:10:56.489
Yeah!

00:11:00.826 --> 00:11:03.746
We ain't got money to buy more drinks.

00:11:03.829 --> 00:11:04.789
Not just that,

00:11:05.331 --> 00:11:08.542
I've got… I'm getting married tomorrow…

00:11:16.425 --> 00:11:17.968
Awesome!

00:11:18.052 --> 00:11:21.055
This is how I survived when I was a kid.

00:11:21.138 --> 00:11:24.809
This is where
the legend of Johnny Bolt started.

00:11:24.892 --> 00:11:26.602
Let's get a little more.

00:11:26.685 --> 00:11:29.105
Yeah, a little more won't hurt.

00:11:29.188 --> 00:11:30.689
-It sure won't!
-It sure won't!

00:11:33.275 --> 00:11:35.111
Say, Johnny,

00:11:35.194 --> 00:11:40.116
don't you think you should make
your last job a big one for Kasey's sake?

00:11:40.199 --> 00:11:43.285
Nah. I'm gonna get married
and work an ordinary--

00:11:43.369 --> 00:11:48.374
Someone once said that money is always
why marriage for love ends in divorce.

00:11:49.708 --> 00:11:51.127
Now, who was it that said that?

00:11:53.212 --> 00:11:54.547
It was my mom!

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:56.257
She was crying when she said it.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:12:01.095
Johnny, you don't want your wife to suffer
'cause you're short on money, right?

00:12:01.178 --> 00:12:04.640
There's a ton of ATMs
on this street alone.

00:12:07.768 --> 00:12:11.105
These new ones all got cameras on 'em!

00:12:13.482 --> 00:12:14.316
Here!

00:12:14.859 --> 00:12:18.446
We thought this might happen,
so we packed these in the car.

00:12:18.529 --> 00:12:20.030
Yeah.

00:12:21.198 --> 00:12:23.784
You gotta pay for
that wedding too, Johnny.

00:12:23.868 --> 00:12:26.495
Just one more time? For Kasey's sake.

00:12:34.044 --> 00:12:36.505
People of San Francisco!

00:12:36.589 --> 00:12:39.008
Good morning!

00:12:48.684 --> 00:12:49.602
Yeah!

00:12:51.395 --> 00:12:52.229
Yeah!

00:12:56.609 --> 00:12:57.443
Here.

00:12:58.944 --> 00:13:02.031
This is the only way to live!

00:13:02.114 --> 00:13:04.742
Nah! I've changed!

00:13:05.326 --> 00:13:08.204
My wonderful honey! I love you!

00:13:08.871 --> 00:13:11.790
Johnny! You should get Kasey a present!

00:13:11.874 --> 00:13:13.292
A present?

00:13:13.876 --> 00:13:15.794
A present for my angel?

00:13:15.878 --> 00:13:18.172
A present for my angel…

00:13:18.255 --> 00:13:20.799
A present for my angel…

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:22.384
That's the place!

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:25.471
A bookstore? How come?

00:13:25.554 --> 00:13:28.557
What does it matter?
Just pull over there, Frostbite!

00:13:29.558 --> 00:13:31.685
But I can't stop this!

00:13:31.769 --> 00:13:33.395
Let there be bad luck!

00:13:49.828 --> 00:13:52.581
That hurts… Why the hell a bookstore?

00:13:53.123 --> 00:13:55.459
For school textbooks for my angel!

00:13:55.543 --> 00:13:56.961
Textbooks?

00:13:57.044 --> 00:13:58.045
That's right.

00:13:58.128 --> 00:14:01.215
She said MBA textbooks
are ridiculously expensive.

00:14:02.925 --> 00:14:03.968
What a dumb present.

00:14:05.636 --> 00:14:07.721
My wife's really smart.

00:14:09.431 --> 00:14:11.850
Shit! It's the cops! Let's scram!

00:14:11.934 --> 00:14:14.687
Grab all the books that say "MBA"!

00:14:20.067 --> 00:14:22.403
I can't let myself get caught!

00:14:26.448 --> 00:14:27.283
Yeah.

00:14:37.084 --> 00:14:37.918
Yeah!

00:14:43.841 --> 00:14:47.177
Stay calm! We don't want to hurt anyone!

00:14:47.761 --> 00:14:49.889
It's an honor to meet you, Praetorian.

00:14:49.972 --> 00:14:51.682
How many robbers are there?

00:14:51.765 --> 00:14:55.352
Four. They got on a train
two stations before this one.

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:58.355
Get a paddy wagon to the next station.

00:14:58.439 --> 00:14:59.773
It'll only take
a few minutes to handle this.

00:15:10.993 --> 00:15:12.328
What shitty luck.

00:15:27.676 --> 00:15:29.887
I can't let myself get caught today!

00:15:31.263 --> 00:15:33.098
I'm going to go straight!

00:15:38.103 --> 00:15:39.688
Honey! Wait for me!

00:16:09.802 --> 00:16:11.553
Another fine achievement.

00:16:12.137 --> 00:16:13.222
Who cares about that?

00:16:13.764 --> 00:16:14.932
You don't either, right?

00:16:15.641 --> 00:16:17.810
What's important is that justice prevails.

00:16:18.394 --> 00:16:19.770
Precisely.

00:16:27.403 --> 00:16:29.279
My sweetheart…

00:16:38.288 --> 00:16:39.123
Yo!

00:16:39.206 --> 00:16:41.208
You're back sooner than I expected.

00:16:41.709 --> 00:16:43.585
Welcome back, Johnny.

00:16:46.922 --> 00:16:49.258
Finally, you're back.

00:16:49.341 --> 00:16:50.968
It's your move, Johnny.

00:16:54.763 --> 00:16:55.973
Eric, please!

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:58.100
Let me make one phone call!

00:16:58.183 --> 00:16:59.810
Today's my wedding day!

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:01.478
Eric!

00:17:01.562 --> 00:17:03.105
Eric!

00:17:16.827 --> 00:17:18.871
Maybe he's on the subway
and has no signal.

00:17:19.913 --> 00:17:21.832
Have all the guests arrived?

00:17:24.793 --> 00:17:30.424
Three guests haven't arrived.
Frostbite, Kismet, and Transmit.

00:17:31.508 --> 00:17:33.135
All right. Thank you.

00:17:57.493 --> 00:18:00.954
"Thanks to you, I was able to change."

00:18:02.831 --> 00:18:04.833
You haven't changed one single bit.

00:18:07.544 --> 00:18:09.463
I wonder what's taking so long.

00:18:42.371 --> 00:18:44.456
Mommy! Those fireworks are so cool!

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:45.958
They sure are!

00:18:46.041 --> 00:18:47.709
Wow!

00:18:57.511 --> 00:18:59.096
Slow down now!

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:05.310
<i>News flash! In the trial of
the former superhero, Praetorian,</i>

00:19:05.394 --> 00:19:09.606
<i>he was pronounced innocent
of the more than 300 counts against him.</i>

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:14.987
<i>He was charged with taking advantage of
his position as a superhero for years</i>

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:18.949
<i>to regularly commit assault,
blackmail, and sell information, but…</i>

00:19:20.242 --> 00:19:22.244
<i>Gladiator has just come outside!</i>

00:19:22.327 --> 00:19:24.830
<i>Since you and Praetorian had
a close relationship,</i>

00:19:24.913 --> 00:19:29.501
<i>opinion on the Internet is that
you were involved in his crimes too.</i>

00:19:29.585 --> 00:19:31.086
<i>Can you comment on that?</i>

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:32.379
<i>Me?</i>

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.048
The hell I was!

00:19:40.262 --> 00:19:43.640
<i>I've always been suspicious
of that Praetorian.</i>

00:19:44.683 --> 00:19:46.226
Innocent my ass!

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:48.520
I heard he hired a super-expensive lawyer.

00:19:49.188 --> 00:19:51.982
That itself is proof
he's in cahoots with criminals.

00:19:52.065 --> 00:19:54.776
Black 28. Another win.

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:56.737
Wow! That's amazing!

00:20:00.073 --> 00:20:03.035
Sir, it looks like your lucky night.

00:20:03.118 --> 00:20:04.328
Fantastic!

00:20:04.411 --> 00:20:06.288
That's nine times in a row!

00:20:06.872 --> 00:20:09.666
Next, I'm putting it all on 18.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:12.377
If I win this,
I'll get to a million dollars.

00:20:12.961 --> 00:20:15.255
All of it, sir? On one number?

00:20:17.216 --> 00:20:20.427
Tonight, I've got lady luck with me!

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:23.180
Hey! Leave me out of this, would you!

00:20:25.515 --> 00:20:27.684
Hurry up and spin it!

00:20:28.518 --> 00:20:31.438
What's going on with table 47?

00:20:31.521 --> 00:20:33.065
He's taken us for 400 grand.

00:20:33.148 --> 00:20:35.192
There's clearly a precog involved.

00:20:35.859 --> 00:20:38.445
We haven't detected the use of
psychic powers inside the casino.

00:20:39.112 --> 00:20:42.783
According to the database,
the gambler is definitely The Heat.

00:20:43.492 --> 00:20:45.994
Comb the entire premises.

00:20:46.078 --> 00:20:48.080
He's definitely up to something.

00:20:51.458 --> 00:20:53.085
Carmine, hurry up and get out of there.

00:20:53.835 --> 00:20:56.755
Turning 50 bucks into
1,2 million is going too far.

00:20:56.838 --> 00:20:58.173
We'll get caught for…

00:20:59.633 --> 00:21:02.302
Would you mind stepping out of the car?

00:21:06.848 --> 00:21:08.475
Carmine, I'm sorry.

00:21:09.059 --> 00:21:11.228
I didn't know what else to do.

00:21:11.311 --> 00:21:13.605
Don't be so hard on yourself.

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:19.069
Your name is Walt Flanagan.
Isn't that right?

00:21:20.195 --> 00:21:21.280
Yes.

00:21:28.078 --> 00:21:32.916
According to the database,
you can see 30 seconds into the future.

00:21:33.709 --> 00:21:34.710
That's right.

00:21:37.462 --> 00:21:39.339
Then I guess you can see

00:21:39.923 --> 00:21:42.968
where this fancy cigar case
will be in 30 seconds, can't you?

00:21:43.927 --> 00:21:44.970
Yes, I can.

00:21:47.347 --> 00:21:48.432
Such a pity.

00:22:13.332 --> 00:22:14.916
Now listen.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:17.627
I admire your balls.

00:22:18.211 --> 00:22:19.755
But this is an excellent chance

00:22:19.838 --> 00:22:23.050
to teach you, low-status villains,
how brutal the organization can be.

00:22:24.051 --> 00:22:26.511
Salamander… I can't breathe!

00:22:26.595 --> 00:22:31.099
Bring me 100 million dollars in one month!

00:22:34.644 --> 00:22:36.980
A hundred million. Got it?

00:22:37.064 --> 00:22:40.150
And don't try to pull anything stupid.

00:22:40.233 --> 00:22:43.361
How in the world
am I supposed to get 100 million dollars?

00:22:43.445 --> 00:22:46.156
How should I know?
Why not try knocking off a bank?

00:22:46.239 --> 00:22:49.993
May as well end your life
as a petty thief with a bang.

00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:12.974
It's only natural you're upset.

00:23:13.058 --> 00:23:14.851
I really am sorry.

00:23:14.935 --> 00:23:16.853
I've got nothing to say to you. Get out.

00:23:17.437 --> 00:23:20.607
I just wanted money to pay for
the wedding. You can understand that.

00:23:21.108 --> 00:23:23.819
I don't want to hear it,
even if you're joking!

00:23:23.902 --> 00:23:27.197
You're the one who said
you wanted to start an ordinary life.

00:23:27.989 --> 00:23:29.533
But you're the one

00:23:29.616 --> 00:23:32.619
who tossed that all away
and ruined our… my future!

00:23:34.329 --> 00:23:37.082
I just thought we'd need
a little more money

00:23:37.165 --> 00:23:38.583
to start an ordinary life.

00:23:38.667 --> 00:23:40.752
Must be nice
not to have to pay rent in prison.

00:23:42.337 --> 00:23:45.215
What are you working in
a coffee shop like this again for?

00:23:45.799 --> 00:23:46.758
What about your MBA?

00:23:46.842 --> 00:23:50.137
With smarts like yours, sweetie,
you shouldn't have to work in a place--

00:23:53.723 --> 00:23:55.684
MBA?

00:23:55.767 --> 00:23:58.103
I punched that groping professor
and got kicked out!

00:23:58.854 --> 00:24:01.231
Smarts? You think I'm smart?

00:24:01.314 --> 00:24:03.441
My grades were horrible the whole time!

00:24:04.067 --> 00:24:08.405
I never even succeeded once
at any big jobs as a villain!

00:24:13.410 --> 00:24:16.663
How dare you suddenly show up
and push your male fantasies on me.

00:24:17.330 --> 00:24:19.708
I failed my MBA.
I failed at being a villain too!

00:24:19.791 --> 00:24:22.836
That's why I'm working
at a coffee shop like this.

00:24:27.132 --> 00:24:27.966
Sweetheart…

00:24:30.051 --> 00:24:30.969
Get out.

00:24:35.974 --> 00:24:37.142
Carmine?

00:24:41.354 --> 00:24:43.231
-Carmine!
-What's wrong?

00:24:43.815 --> 00:24:46.401
Johnny… Kasey…

00:24:47.402 --> 00:24:49.696
I need help…

00:26:13.488 --> 00:26:18.493
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
